0..78 Comment "// A family applied at a call\'s result converts with itself. A type that reads"
79..152 Comment "// a call\'s value runs the call first and binds it, so `tm(extend(g))` is"
153..224 Comment "// `c ← extend(g); tm(c)`; a dependent arrow instantiated at the call"
225..302 Comment "// `extend(g)` binds it ahead of each code that reads the binder, so the type"
303..369 Comment "// it yields is written the same way. The shape is a category with"
370..447 Comment "// families: operations over context extension, laws that apply one operation"
448..520 Comment "// to another\'s result (Dybjer, _Internal Type Theory_, TYPES 1995, LNCS"
521..596 Comment "// 1158). The same law stated as a record\'s field reads the record\'s family"
597..664 Comment "// field by its label in every type it prints. A record holding the"
665..743 Comment "// family and an operation into it checks the operation at the family it holds"
744..815 Comment "// , and its operation\'s type prints as the arrow the family\'s argument"
816..825 Comment "// drops."
826..828 Comment "//"
829..864 Comment "// - see: #720 — `useAtExtension`"
865..893 Comment "// - see: #728 — `fieldAt`"
894..927 Comment "// - see: #721 — `familyRecord`"
928..961 Comment "// - see: #736 — `familyRecord`"
962..1001 Comment "// - see: #2751 — `appliedWrittenOut`"
1003..1080 Comment "/// A family applied to an operation\'s result, met at one argument: `q(g)` is"
1081..1151 Comment "/// at `tm(extend(g))`, which is `use`\'s second domain at `extend(g)`."
